WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.730
<b>Autumn Moon
Ohagi</b>

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.730
For the week around the spring ohigan equinox,
 it's called "botamochi," after peony flowers.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>Ohagi (Chunky An • Kinako)</b>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>piece</b>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>yen</b>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>pieces</b>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>yen</b>

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:07.720
During the fall ohigan equinox,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.640
it's called "ohagi," after the flowers 
of the bush clover.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.790
Even though they're the same thing,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.990
the name changes depending on the season.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.220
Which name's the right one?

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.940
Both of them.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.120
Excuse me, is anyone there?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.750
Yes, coming!

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.090
Maeda-obachan!

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.250
Nagomu-chan! I'm sorry to 
come when you're so busy.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.370
Here, I've brought a program.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.550
A program?

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.880
It's for the district sports festival.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.300
63rd
<b>Miyama School District Sports Festival
</b>on the Kitayama Elementary School grounds

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.300
Wow...

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.610
If you'll take care of that for me?

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.220
Oh, yes, I will.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.440
The district sports festival, huh?

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.410
That's right, I remember these.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:53.900
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:21.780
<b>Autumn's Potato Moon</b>

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.600
Itsuka-chan!

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.490
Hm?

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.330
Are you going to be in the sports festival?

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.290
I've got cram school in the afternoon, 
so I'm only doing the morning events.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:31.120
I'm doing the whole thing. My dad and 
older brother are really excited about it.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.300
We probably have work, 
so I'm not sure if I will.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.630
Oh, right. The shop is open 
on Sundays, too, isn't it?

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:44.320
Plus, last year, the old man hurt his back,
 and they had to call an ambulance.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.640
<i>I can't! I can't go on! Take down
 my last words! Lawyer!</i>

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.680
The thing where he broke the tape 
at the finish line even as he fell.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.600
And he got the award for 
fighting spirit, didn't he?

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:52.620
Mako-chan, what time does your 
class start? What will you do for lunch?

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.480
I'll have a bento somewhere 
in the neighborhood.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.470
Then let's all eat together!

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.740
You, too, Itsuka-chan!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.240
Y-Yeah. If I can make it.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.160
<i>Whole families enter together,</i>

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.250
<i>competing against others in the neighborhood.
 The district sports festival...</i>

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.900
<i>When I was still with Papa, he had 
work and stuff, so I couldn't enter.</i>

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.840
<b>Kaminoyama</b>

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.840
<i>Last year with Ryokushou was
 the first time I was in it.</i>

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.590
<i>Running with my friends...</i>

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.390
<b>Tricycle Battle
 600m Relay
  50m Dash
 200m Relay
 400m Relay
Dekapan Relay</b>

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.390
<b>Pre-schoolers
 General, 6 total, male & female
 Seniors
 Elementary grades 1, 2, 3
 Elementary grades 4, 5, 6
 Parent and child</b>

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.390
<i>Playing together until it 
was time for our events...</i>

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.260
<i>It was all fun, but...</i>

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.480
<i>I can't let myself look dejected!</i>

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.190
<i>After all, I might not even be able to enter.</i>

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.950
I'm back!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.410
Welcome home!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.620
63rd
<b>Miyama School District Sports Festival
</b> on the Kitayama Elementary School grounds

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.620
Which event are you entering?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.620
This year, the whole family's entering again!

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.310
And we'll go cheer for you.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.630
Do your best out there.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.630
B-But what about work?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.590
The tea shops are closed that day.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.030
We'll be busy right through 
the day before, though.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.040
This year we have young master 
Nagomu, so we can go all out!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.310
That aside... Itsuka, mark the 
events you want to compete in.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.280
O-Okay.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:23.320
<b>Kick Race
 Faster than the Wind
 Ball Toss

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:23.320
<b>Afternoon</b>

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:23.320
<b>No restrictions
 Pre-schoolers
 No restrictions

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.820
Fifth graders' 50 meter dash...

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.320
The combined relay...

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.070
<b>Parent and child</b>

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.620
The dekapan race...

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.230
Did you want to enter that?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.980
We didn't have that one 
back when I was in these.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.420
Oh, no, I—

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.290
It's limited to parent-child entries, huh?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.730
But we're basically like parent and child,

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.800
so I don't think anyone would mind 
if you entered with me, right?

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.800
Oh. I see. That's a no. No, huh?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.230
I'm going to go do my homework.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:46.550
Work hard!

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.390
Welcome home.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.710
What happened?

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:56.310
I shouldn't have said we're 
like parent and child.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.150
The way things have been going, 
I thought it might work.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.910
I'm sorry, Nagomu.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.450
It's all because I asked you 
to be like a father to her.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.140
Did you say that to me?

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.200
That forgetfulness of yours 
is one of your good points.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.560
I just...

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.140
I want to tell her that she 
isn't alone. That's all.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.170
<b>Program</b>

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.170
<b> 

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.170
<b> 

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.170
<b>Afternoon</b>

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.100
Good morning.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.960
This year, we are once again able 
to commence our sports festival.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.220
63rd
<b> Miyama School District Sports Festival</b>

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:32.040
This year, Kitayama Elementary School has 
happily lent us their sports grounds again.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.950
Thank you very much for that.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:38.230
<b>Chanotsuji</b>

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:40.010
And now, I declare the 63rd Miyama 
School District Sports Festival open!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.280
The first things on our program are 
the elementary school foot races.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.700
<b>Kaminoyama</b>

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.950
Itsuka!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.740
Give it everything you've got!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.570
What d'you think, Itsuka?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.230
Koume and Yuume want to run too!

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.300
Run!

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.790
Yes, yes. There's a sprint that 
all the little ones can enter,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.160
even if they're not from the neighborhood.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.460
Yay!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.010
Make five lines in order, all right?

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.460
<b>Ichiyama</b>

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.560
Hey, Yukihira.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.340
Noi-kun.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.100
I lost last year, but this year I'm gonna win.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.730
What's with the 
"this-is-deeply-exhausting" face?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.070
<i>I don't care about winning or losing.</i>

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.410
<i>It's not like I have family to watch anyway.</i>

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.490
Ready...

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.020
Itsuka!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.050
You can do it!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.990
<b>Itsuka Fight!</b>

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.320
You can do it!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:39.160
<b>Fight! Itsuka</b>

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.160
You can do it!

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.880
Yeah!

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:52.640
Hey, Yukihira!

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.940
You'd better come out for the bat-spin next!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.390
Itsuka-chan, congratulations!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.390
<b>Kousaiji</b>

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.390
I came in fourth!

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:02.600
Itsuka-chan, I thought your 
parents were away on business,

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.120
and that's why you live at the wagashi shop,

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.090
but I was wrong, right?

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:06.650
Huh?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.870
Your dad shouted really loud.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.320
H-He's not my dad!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.610
Really?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.120
<b>Kaminoyama Neighborhood</b>

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.120
Itsuka, welcome back. Congratulations!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.830
Welcome back, Itsuka! 
Could you hear me cheering?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.330
Please don't do it again.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.840
Okay. Next, I'm gonna show 
Itsuka how good I can be!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.240
First place, the Kaminoyama District.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.840
<b>Kaminoyama</b>

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.590
What do you think, Itsuka?

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:33.840
She's not there!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.700
Nagomu!

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.660
It's been a while! You're looking good.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.450
Nacchan! Kazuyan!

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.960
If you're back, you should've gotten in touch.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.450
Sorry.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.720
You're helping at your parents' place, 
right? What about your guitar?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:55.640
I play sometimes.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.130
Is the girl you were cheering for 
the one who's staying with you?

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.570
I heard that her parents aren't around, 
so Ryokushou's taking care of her, right?

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.800
That must be tough.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.290
She's not even related to you, right?

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:09.480
It's not like that. Itsuka's a 
precious member of my family.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:15.890
<b>Kaminoyama      Nishitsu</b>

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.430
Wow!

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.690
It was Masa-san and Saki-kun.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:33.200
They brought us some ohagi for a snack.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.950
Next we have the senior 
division's 50 meter dash.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.700
All right!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.330
<b>Kaminoyama</b>

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.860
This is where...

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.740
we'll finish things.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.460
Otousan!

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.710
Is this a comedy skit?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.040
What do we do?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.320
He entered the last event, 
the parent-child dekapan race.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.220
Huh? Who's he entered with?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.070
With you.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.470
I never heard anything about it!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:02.470
They were short one team, so he entered.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.850
Honestly, at his age...

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.000
But I'm pretty worn out, too.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.640
It seems impossible at this point.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.180
Here.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:13.740
Huh?

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.490
Hey! It's ohagi!

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:22.940
Anko has iron, polyphenols, and dietary fiber,
 and they're good for a tired body.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.710
Someone said that to me once.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.000
You said that if you entered with me, 
we'd be like parent and child, right?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.630
Mom...

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.510
Hm?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.880
Please give me all the ohagi that are left.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.510
What?

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.510
On your marks!

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:44.520
<b>Kaminoyama</b>

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.640
Are you all right?

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.520
I'm totally fine.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.350
Here we go, Itsuka.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.640
Ready...

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.990
63rd
<b> Miyama School District Sports Festival</b>

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.840
Look! We got the award for 
best parent and child!

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.480
Well, you were perfectly in sync.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:02.990
That's great!

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.450
Itsuka! Let's take a 
picture to remember this!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.160
I'll make it my wallpaper!

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.490
I don't want to.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.210
Oh, come on, Itsuka!

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.670
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.670
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:21.260
<b>Ohagi</b>

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.870
Welcome!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.260
Excuse me...

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:25.020
Is there a girl named Yukihira Itsuka here?

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.490
What did you say?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.070
Oh, what should we do?

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:31.520
For now, I'll come back before everyone else.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.630
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.460
What is it? Something wrong?

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:39.780
What?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.550
Itsuka's... mother?

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.040
Where's Itsuka?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:53.790
She must have been tired. After all,
 she did do amazingly well.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.560
She's fast asleep.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.300
After the sports festival,

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:06.560
I spoke with Itsuka's mother a little, but...

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.810
I asked if she might come back 
again tomorrow afternoon.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.240
What?

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.430
Let me just say that what 
you're eating right now

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.570
are snacks that she gave us.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:24.310
I mean... suddenly being told 
she'll be coming here...

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:38.590
Then, today you'll meet up with Mitsuru-chan 
and do your homework there, all right?

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.850
Yes. I'll be going now.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.910
Bye. Be safe.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.850
I'm going now.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.740
Be careful out there!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.870
Enough already! Please go back inside!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.620
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.620
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.380
I'm sorry for intruding 
so suddenly yesterday.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.130
Pleased to meet you. 
My name is Yukihira Shinri.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.890
I am Itsuka's mother.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.800
<i>She's really her mother.</i>

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:36.150
I'm the master of Ryokushou, Irino Heigo.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.100
Hey!

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.220
I'm his son, Nagomu.

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.040
Where is Itsuka?

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.240
She's still at school.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.890
And since this is all so sudden, 
we haven't told her we're doing this.

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:50.870
I understand.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.380
I would like to formally thank you
 for looking after Itsuka.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.560
Oh, no. Please, raise your head.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.740
And, well, we'd be happy 
to keep Itsuka with us...

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.740
I'd like to cut straight to the point.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.430
I've come to collect Itsuka.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.340
<i>Of course she has.</i>

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.680
I've been looking for her all this time.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.080
My husband and I have been
 separated for five years.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:18.690
Right now, I live with my parents in France.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:22.190
But I've never forgotten her,
 not even for a moment.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:27.200
I'd planned to leave her with my husband 
just until I settled in over there.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.710
Separated? He said you'd broken up.

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.010
We do plan to divorce...

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:35.660
But we decided to leave it at "separated" 
until Itsuka comes of age.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.920
My husband's work takes 
him from place to place,

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.960
so it was difficult to contact him.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:46.010
And for the last year or so, even that 
communication had broken off completely.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:51.720
So I hired a detective agency 
who eventually pointed me here.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:51.720
<b>Yukihira-sama</b>

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:51.720
<b>Investigation Report</b>

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.780
An investigation report?

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.690
I also had them investigate Ryokushou.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.530
They said that, in spite of the fact 
that my husband thrust her upon you,

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.900
you've treated her like part of your family.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.240
Of course Itsuka's part of the family.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:09.120
She said that she'd inherit 
Ryokushou one day.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.120
She will not.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:09.990
What?

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:15.000
At my side, Itsuka will live a life with 
a much broader outlook. That is my intent.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.830
More importantly, if you need an heir, 
you have your son there, don't you?

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.260
Huh? Where?

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.840
Could you please not deny that right now?

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:27.610
And an adult who's been a wastrel for 
ten years will be a bad influence on her.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:32.600
I beg of you. Please allow me to see Itsuka.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.990
I'll go pack up Itsuka's things.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.360
Otousan...

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:04.110
Um... Where did you meet Itsuka's father?

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:04.940
Huh?

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:09.170
I just... I play guitar too, 
so I was wondering what he's like.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:11.630
<i>That look is the same as Itsuka's!</i>

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:14.140
For now, let me say, I'm sorry.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.600
Kind. Friendly.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.110
And utterly useless.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.910
It's a common story.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:25.680
He had qualities I thought were cute 
when we were dating

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:29.900
that, once we were married, I realized 
were the qualities of a spoiled child.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.240
I've always loved working,

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.090
so I worked really hard 
as the family's main support.

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:39.660
But everything just slipped further 
and further from what I'd hoped for.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.250
<i>Itsuka...</i>

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.320
Mama's going to go sort of far away.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:48.920
So you should come with me, too.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:53.240
The one going with you 
isn't Itsuka, it's Work, right?

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.460
Bye-bye!

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.060
My heart broke.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.060
Yeah, it would break.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.960
You must have wondered why 
I've never visited until now.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.740
No, I never...

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.310
I really could have visited at any time.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.870
But the thought of Itsuka right there,

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.830
saying "bye-bye" to me again... it scared me.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:21.170
"There's no one by her side right now."

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.680
"I want to help her, to be her strength."

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:28.090
I want to get back the time I lost
 through my lack of courage.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.340
Don't worry.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.390
You're parent and child, right?

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.810
Itsuka never asks anyone for anything.

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:45.350
I think it's because, deep in her heart, 
she knows who it is she should be asking.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:49.500
Go make Itsuka a "spoiled child."

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.870
<b>Open</b>

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.870
<b>This Month's Special Menu!!</b>

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.870
<b>Tsukimi Dango</b>

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:14.630
Sorry, Itsuka-chan. I'm going 
to step away for a minute.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.470
Huh? Okay.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.420
I'm sorry.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:39.900
Mama?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.120
Thanks, Mitsuru-chan.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:54.700
Let's go.

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.550
Are you sure, Nagomu-san?

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.480
I'm sure.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.170
I'm sorry.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:08.560
Mama didn't have the courage 
to come see you, Itsuka.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.940
Shall we order something? You must be hungry.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:17.060
What should we get?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.230
Tsukimi dango.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:23.500
Tonight's the 15th night, 
the Autumn Moon.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.130
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.100
These are tsukimi dango?

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.590
They aren't shaped like the ones I know.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:38.350
In Kanto, they're shaped 
to resemble the moon,

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:41.450
but in Kansai, they're shaped 
like satoimo potatoes.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:45.980
The Autumn Moon is a time to 
give thanks for the harvest,

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:50.110
but the thing that's in season at the 
time happens to be satoimo potatoes,

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:52.250
so that's what the mochi part of this is.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:55.200
The anko represents the clouds,

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.320
and they say the whole thing is meant 
to look like the moon hidden by clouds.

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:01.320
You certainly know a lot.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.380
Papa taught me. He didn't 
tell you about them, Mama?

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:08.040
I'm not sure.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.950
Papa said that he learned 
from the old man at Ryokushou.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.290
Wagashi is fun, right?

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.000
I want to know even more.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.420
More about the wagashi that Papa loves.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:25.560
Are you having fun right now?

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.910
Yes, lots of fun!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:32.470
Mama, thank you for coming to see me.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.240
It's already eight, isn't it?

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.180
Take a look, Nagomu.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.440
It's a beautiful moon.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:51.830
Kaguya-hime went home 
to that beautiful place.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:58.340
It was fun. I felt like I had a daughter.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.240
That should be "granddaughter," shouldn't it?

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:03.340
I'm not giving you any dango.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.460
<i>Itsuka's going away.</i>

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:12.200
<i>When they say "a hole 
opened up in my heart,"</i>

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.260
<i>I wonder if this is the feeling they mean.</i>

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.000
<i>And back when I left for Tokyo...</i>

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:22.230
<i>I wonder if this is how Mom and Dad felt.</i>

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.370
Coming!

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:30.420
I'm back!

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.000
Y-Y...

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:33.640
Itsuka!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:34.780
What happened?!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.670
I'm sorry I'm so late. 
We talked for a long time.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.220
No, not that. You were with your mother...

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.260
Right?

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:46.320
I'm sorry. We're very late.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.270
Itsuka told me.

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:00.920
Itsuka, aren't you lonely?

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.350
Without Papa and Mama with you...

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.100
I was lonely, but...

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:11.310
Now, everyone at Ryokushou is there for me.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:13.540
And they never let me feel alone.

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:16.040
They say I'm part of the family.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.340
I like it here!

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.900
People she knows she can ask for anything...

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.810
It seems she has them here, too.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.630
I'm going!

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:44.940
Stay sa— Oh!

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.080
Itsuka!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:55.930
You traded contact info 
with Itsuka-chan's mother?

00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:56.990
Yeah.

00:21:56.990 --> 00:21:59.480
After all, we can't give Itsuka a smartphone.

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:01.840
So I'm giving updates in her place.

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:05.880
I was told to send info about what 
Itsuka's doing and pictures of her.

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:07.990
It's a huge responsibility.

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:09.590
The problem is...

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:13.520
Even when she looks at 
the camera, she won't smile for me.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:14.730
Really?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:16.280
She just looks a little shy to me.

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:19.450
Saki-kun, you're so kind.

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>"Dancing in Autumn Colors"</b>

00:23:53.250 --> 00:23:54.620
Perfect.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:00.120
My dream is to become a wagashi artisan.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:01.620
That's so old-school!

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.090
I'm probably the only one having fun.
